{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And he said, to build</b> — for the woman who is inside the ephah." "<b>A house in the land of Shinar</b> — for there they will detain her by force, because of the iniquity that she did not wish to come for the building of the Temple." "<b>And the word והניחה is a compound of והונחה and הניחה, like: 'She dwells in Lebanon, wailing among the cedars' — they pressed me, and many likewise."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {2 "The phrase after the biblical analogy is cryptic; the Hebrew reads צמתותוני ורבים ככה, translated hyper-literally as it stands. The syntax and referent are obscure and may reflect a textual corruption or truncated quotation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:07.322564870Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}